    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>\u201cYou\u2019re trapped in a dream. And the only way out is to go deeper in.\u201d</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Have you ever had a nightmare, where you knew you were dreaming\u2026 but couldn\u2019t wake up?<br>Same operating system. Same browser. Same illegal websites.<br>But something\u2019s off.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >And then you start to remember. And then you start to panic.<br>The line between dream and reality fades as you search for an exit.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Welcome back to the Deep Web.</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It\u2019s changed. Broken. Infected by your own subconscious. <br>You don\u2019t know how to escape. You don\u2019t even know if escape is real.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Project DeepWeb: Eternal Nightmare</strong> is a deep web exploration adventure \u2014 a standalone spinoff of <i>Project DeepWeb</i>. Inspired by Internet lore and subconscious fears, this game tells a story based on a deep and forgotten folklore.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Immersive desktop simulation</strong>. Apps, websites, files \u2014 all twisted by the dream</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >New applications, new content, an entirely new experience</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Uncover dozens of new puzzles</strong>, encrypted websites, and lost data fragments</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Discover new corners of the deep internet</strong>, now even darker</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>New horror tropes: </strong>investigate the internet\u2019s most forbidden secrets \u2014 even the ones that were meant to stay buried.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>The Show\u2019s over. Time to wake up.</strong></h2>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><i>\u201cYou\u2019re trapped in a dream. And the only way out is to go deeper in.\u201d</i></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Have you ever had a nightmare, where you knew you were dreaming\u2026 but couldn\u2019t wake up?<br>Same operating system. Same browser. Same illegal websites.<br>But something\u2019s off.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >And then you start to remember. And then you start to panic.<br>The line between dream and reality fades as you search for an exit.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Welcome back to the Deep Web.</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It\u2019s changed. Broken. Infected by your own subconscious. <br>You don\u2019t know how to escape. You don\u2019t even know if escape is real.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Project DeepWeb: Eternal Nightmare</strong> is a deep web exploration adventure \u2014 a standalone spinoff of <i>Project DeepWeb</i>. Inspired by Internet lore and subconscious fears, this game tells a story based on a deep and forgotten folklore.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Immersive desktop simulation</strong>. Apps, websites, files \u2014 all twisted by the dream</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >New applications, new content, an entirely new experience</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Uncover dozens of new puzzles</strong>, encrypted websites, and lost data fragments</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Discover new corners of the deep internet</strong>, now even darker</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>New horror tropes: </strong>investigate the internet\u2019s most forbidden secrets \u2014 even the ones that were meant to stay buried.</p></li></ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>The Show\u2019s over. Time to wake up.</strong></h2>",
